  "live_records": {
    "q-51768": {
      "dom_id": "step-q51768",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the set of values of $w$ that satisfy $w-3\\le -1$ or $5w>25.$ Express your answer in interval notation.",
      "worked_solution": "We start by solving $w-3\\le -1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-3+3 & \\le -1+3 \\\\ w & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/41894afbf397505568367e80d14e34fe2b04a2acdfd5398bd8ba41727b8c67c6.png)\n\nThen, we solve $5w>25:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5w}{5} & >\\frac{25}{5} \\\\ w & >5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/262a3e683cb8c8a67cdd58c0f138e44466c346092c7f74ec03ec1483a385056a.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $w$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/95d67331522c16093207de451a33bb713b42e1418d1f4c1a7aa1ef6369a51e4b.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $w\\le 2$ or $w>5.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,2]\\cup (5,\\infty ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
