    "q-28961": {
      "dom_id": "step-q28961",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $3x+5>14$ or $2x-3\\le 1.$ Express your answer in interval notation.",
      "worked_solution": "We start by solving $3x+5>14:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+5 & >14 \\\\ 3x & >9 \\\\ x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/5dca213f8266a9bd001380b30368e5996b24fa2ddb6d3aef5670befde451e77d.png)\n\nThen, we solve $2x-3\\le 1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & \\le 1 \\\\ 2x & \\le 4 \\\\ x & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/454e1de1e32bb5e3fb03dc280076414493d9e4a9c042246be565d8550c2012f2.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/531c59b67623a10db6af4236187e7d50315e7068585d6a5e6882db0d1997bdce.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 2$ or $x>3.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,2]\\cup (3,\\infty ).\\,\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
